v 3
d 'HETSET': module for partial identification of heterogeneous treatment effects across settings
d
d  hetset implements the partial identification framework of
d  Huntington-Klein (2026, arXiv:2605.25483) for causal effects that
d  vary across settings (subgroups). Effects are estimated separately
d  by setting, with omitted-variable-bias plausibility intervals from
d  sensemakr (Cinelli, Ferwerda, and Hazlett). Researchers then bound
d  rho, the proportional relationship between the bias in one setting
d  and another, and hetset uses linear programming to check whether an
d  identified set of effects exists and to report the per-setting
d  bounds implied by all restrictions jointly. A Stata port of the R
d  package of the same name.
d
d  Requires: Stata version 14 (version 16 for identified_set_exists
d  and univariate_bounds_table, which use the Mata LinearProgram()
d  class).
d
d  Required package: sensemakr (from SSC).
d
d  Distribution-Date: 20260610
d
d  Author: Nick Huntington-Klein, Seattle University
d  Support: email nhuntington-klein@@seattleu.edu
d
